module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.bare_name_resolved_only_by_the_flat_namespace

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data bare_name_resolved_only_by_the_flat_namespace: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "bare_name_resolved_only_by_the_flat_namespace" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "**a bare name resolved only by the flat namespace** (INVALID STATE: a module names a provider or type bare -- `systemd.Journalctl.UnitInvocationLog(...)`, `ConstructionJustification { ... }` -- without importing its declaring module. Every whole-tree compile resolves it, because that compile's single flat namespace already holds the declaring module. An entry compiled ALONE loads only its import closure, the declaring module is not pulled, and the entry refuses (`no field 'Journalctl' on type 'systemd'`, `unresolved type 'ConstructionJustification'`).",

    "HARM: SILENT UNTIL DISPATCH. Every required lane compiles a whole-tree or floor subject, so all of them stay green. The operational workflow entry `gunbc.runner.runner_microvm_slot_start` (fleet-converge mode microvm_slot_start) sat uncompilable on main, and would have refused the next time it was dispatched to a host. The severity lives in (check x population that executes it): the refusal is loud, but no CI step compiles the population it fires in.",

    "MECHANISM: the loader's bare-reference channel, rostered as `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` `bare_reference_channel_declines_a_pull_in_silence`: a file that declares any `import` line has its bare channel turned off, so a bare use in such a file never pulls the declaring module. That row owns the loader mechanism. This row owns the POPULATION gap: separately compiled entries that no CI step compiles on their own.",

    "RECEIPTS: gunbc#12158 added `runner_microvm_lifecycle_realize` `observe_guest_bring_up` calling `systemd.Journalctl` bare, and CI stayed green. gunbc#12205 made an unimported bare provider refuse at the file, and seeded this pair as `ActiveDebt` in `v2.workflow.floor_unimported_bare_provider_debt_roster`. A debt row admits the pair; it does not make the name resolve, so the entry still refused. quiet-eagle-13's per-entry census (gunbc#12398) found it together with three siblings: `v2.lens.languages_consumer_census`, `gunbc.auth.patterns` and `gunbc.tools.review_codex`. gunbc#12494 imports the two live ones and retires both pairs with `ImportsFixed`.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: one entry, two compiles, only the scope varying. The whole-root compile is clean. `gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <entry> --target dag --output-dir <tmp>` refuses at the bare site (per quiet-eagle-13's census, gunbc#12398). Receipted on gunbc#12494 (per-entry compile at its reviewed head, one binary, the before side being that head with only the added imports reverted): each entry refused rc=1 without its import and compiled rc=0 with it, with no further refusal exposed.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder for this population -- a located refusal exists, but no gate executes it over the population where it fires. CEILING: 2 for the population (a required per-entry compile over every separately compiled entry) and 3 for the class (a bare name that resolves only through the flat namespace refuses at the file on every route, which gunbc#12205 began by rostering the standing pairs as monotone debt).",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, as the capability: every `gunbc.ci.ci_spec` workflow entry is compiled per-entry by a required phase of an existing required lane -- sufficient that an entry which refuses on its own blocks a merge. The design is a floor phase over the entries derived from `gunbc.ci.ci_spec`, with no new job. The trigger is gated on measuring the fold's price first (eager-owl-205, 2026-09-28): the phase runs on every floor, and one per-entry compile over the microvm closure OOMed and timed out on BuildBuddy.",
    "THE CASE WITH NO IMPORT TO ADD: CONSTRUCTORS OF THE `T?` SUGAR (found on gunbc#13048). extdeps.external_authority `cited_figure_read_obligation(..) -> NonEmptyStr?` returns bare `Absent` and `Present { value: o }`, and no dag/extdeps module imports either name. The seed binds them; the v2 resolver does not: the module's own native resolve refuses resolve_reason_unbound_symbol with resolve_unbound_name_is_declared_in_several_modules at `Absent` (measured through #13028's closure-provider refusal roster, the only refused root in a 15-module std closure). The v2 std modules that did the same had an import to add (v2.std.optional Optional/Present/Absent, #13048), but a module that writes only `T?` names no Optional at all, so for it the language must answer the question this row has not had to: DOES THE `T?` SUGAR BRING ITS CONSTRUCTORS INTO SCOPE, and if so, WHICH declaration do they bind to when several modules declare a Present/Absent? Until that is decided, every dag/extdeps module that constructs or matches a `T?` value refuses its own v2 resolve and drops out of any closure index that needs it. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: a declared binding of the `?` sugar's constructors (to one Optional authority) that v2 resolve consults -- or a ruling that `T?` users must import that authority, with the import then added -- SUFFICIENT FOR extdeps.external_authority to resolve natively.",
    "RECEIPT (gunbc#13378, 2026-10-05), A WORSE SHAPE OF THIS CLASS: SILENT BIND TO A DIFFERENT CONTRACT, AND A BELOW-FLOOR TYPING GAP. With the v1 seed builtin from_code_point deleted and std.unicode.scalar from_code_point (Int -> Result<String, NotUnicodeScalar>) declared, unmigrated callers that never import it -- e.g. gunbc.namespace_step0_subject_collector step0_subject_paths_at, split(s: paths_nul, delimiter: from_code_point(0)) -- did NOT refuse as unbound: the whole-tree flat namespace bound the bare name to the new partial declaration. The seed then ACCEPTED a Result where split declares String (the ordinary compiler floor: values inhabit declared types) and refused only at EVAL, `gunbc run --entry dag/gunbc/instruments/generated_artifact_gate.dag --function main_wet` -> `TypeError { msg: \"split expects a string argument, got Variant\" }`. So a bare caller is not reliably unbound when a same-named declaration exists anywhere in the pool, and the type mismatch it creates is caught by evaluation, not by inference. v1 is semantics-frozen (gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing), so this is recorded rather than fixed there; the remedy for this population is the migration itself, and the evidence that no caller binds this way is the UnimportedBareProvider floor refusal plus a bare-channel resolve over the out-of-gate modules.",

    "RECEIPT (gunbc#14155, 2026-10-18, W7 build-cache ensure) — THE SAME CHANNEL, A POPULATION WHERE THE ROW'S OWN REFUSAL NEVER FIRES. gunbc.host.sccache_verified_install `sccache_verified_install_admitted_plan` annotated its return type `VerifiedBinaryInstallPlan` while importing three SIBLING names from gunbc.host.verified_binary_install and NOT that one; review 81885 found it by reading. The strict per-entry closure compile — the very gate this row's DISTINGUISHING FACTS credits with refusing — came back `exit=0 blocking=0 unresolved=0` with the import absent. THE DISCRIMINATOR, run on the runner at head 099210da4a0 in one dispatch (four compiles of the same entry — baseline, arm A, arm B, restored — log sizes 6057/6058/6061/6057 lines, so no verdict rests on a truncated log). BOTH arms delete the `VerifiedBinaryInstallPlan,` import line; they differ in exactly ONE respect, which is what makes the pair decisive. ARM A additionally renames the annotation to `VerifiedBinaryInstallPlanZzzNoSuchType`, a type present nowhere in the tree -> `exit=1`, 2 resolution diagnostics, `unresolved type 'VerifiedBinaryInstallPlanZzzNoSuchType'`. ARM B leaves the annotation as written -> `exit=0`, 0 diagnostics. Had annotations been unchecked, ARM A would have been green exactly like ARM B; it was not, so the annotation position IS resolved and explanation 'a strict closure compile never looks at annotation names' is dead. The two arms together locate the mechanism exactly as this row does — the loader's bare-reference channel binding a name through a module it has already loaded — with one distinguishing fact: in this population the declaring module IS in the closure, pulled by a sibling name in the same import block, so the pull is never declined and NO COMPILE ANYWHERE refuses. This is therefore strictly harder to catch than the row's named population, where the per-entry compile refuses loudly: a missing import survives main indefinitely and is found only by a human reader. RECOGNITION RULE, WIDENED: a bare name binds when ANY import in the file pulls its declaring module, whether or not the name itself is listed; a per-entry compile stays green over the whole gap, so legibility of the dependency edge is the only defense until the channel itself refuses.",

    "DISPOSITION, SOURCE LAYOUT CUTOVER (gunbc.plans.source_layout_authority, epoch C2). The debt roster named above, its verdict module and the seed's `unimported_bare_provider_gate` are DELETED: the gate had no executing route since the floor lane was deleted on 2026-10-09 (`gunbc.rung_drop` `v1_required_lanes_withdrawn`), so the roster tracked pairs nothing judged. On a cut-over route the class is now refused where it is used: the acquirer requests only what a module's own text names (an import line, a qualified reference), a bare name is not requestable (R1), and the v2 resolver refuses it unbound with the spelling, the local module and its visible imports named, nothing consulting the repository. The `T?` question above is ruled in the plan's decision table: the sugar's constructors need `import std.optional`. THE POPULATION THAT COVERS is every module a cut-over compile route reaches (R11); outside it the seed still binds a bare name by its ancestor chain and no required step judges that, which `v1_required_lanes_withdrawn` already declares.",
    "RECEIPT (valiant-wren-802, 2026-10-21), A LIVE INSTANCE AT A VARIANT NAME: the guarantee-stall collapse introduced `gunbc.rung_climb` `GroundingAuthority = Declared { reference } | Undeclared`, and bare `Declared` collides with the variant `Declared` of `v2.extdeps.languages.llvm_ir`. With the short arms the rfm-rung-census refused with `missing required field rung in literal of type RecurringFailureMode` on `a_probe_whose_unit_never_ran_is_scored_as_the_forbidden_effect_refused`, a row that states its rung: a misreport located at the wrong declaration. Renaming the arms to `GroundingDeclared`/`GroundingUndeclared` removed it. That rename is the stated AVOIDANCE for this site and does not fix the class, which stays at the rung above.",

    "POPULATION RECEIPT, 2026-10-21 (decl-ref-census, gunbc#14598): the census label //gunbc/instruments:decl-ref-census is the producer. It counts a DeclarationRef constructor whose head has no import row in its own module as bare_heads, and its first run measured 28 such sites in 12 modules. Each resolved only because name resolution is by global uniqueness, not imports. The 12 modules are the evidence references below, by module identity; each now imports its DeclarationRef head and the census refuses a bare head by name. The harm is this row's: a module compiled alone would refuse where the whole-tree compile stays green. This is a different row from an_unimported_bare_name_binds_differently_per_realization, whose harm is one name binding to two functions across realizations; here the name had one binding and only the declaring import was missing.",

    "CALL-SITE RECEIPT, 2026-10-23 (merry-hawk-432, measured at origin/main 1acf79a8 on the remote runner, one dispatch per run): three callers named a cross-module FUNCTION with no import of its owner, and the seed's constructor-reference admission (`constructor_declaration_for_admission` -> `symbol_index_lookup`) refused each as `no declaration is indexed at '<owner>.<name>'`, so `enforcement_consistency_gate_holds` and `cost_coverage_smoke_totality_holds` failed at closure diagnostics before any witness ran. The sites, by identity: `v2.lens.enforcement.cost_coverage` `judge_subject_node` (owner `v2.lens.enforcement.receipts`) and `asymptotic_class_of_cost` (owner `v2.lens.cost`); `v2.lens.complexity_lowering` `asymptotic_class_of_cost`; `v2.lens.enforcement.inventory` `witness_consumer_cadence_for_row` (owner `v2.workflow.witness_admission`). Control: adding exactly the owner imports moved cost_coverage_smoke_totality_holds from exit 1 to PASS and moved enforcement_consistency_gate_holds from a closure refusal to a run. This is the same class as the DeclarationRef bare heads above, at a function call rather than a constructor head: the name had one binding and only the declaring import was missing.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_microvm_lifecycle_realize", decl_name: "observe_guest_bring_up", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.ci.ci_input_envelope", decl_name: "gunbc_ci_corpus_envelope_ceiling_scaffold", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.cli_run_floor_lens_oracle_scaffold", decl_name: "cli_run_floor_lens_read_refusal_hand_rust_scaffold", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.cli_run_workspace_root_scaffold", decl_name: "cli_run_workspace_root_discovery_scaffold", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.hand_lens_host_bridge_scaffold_index", decl_name: "transport_script_position_host_bridge_dissolution_trigger", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.host.host_converge_delta", decl_name: "gunbc_converge_target_byte_normalization_marker", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.language_source_scaffold_index", decl_name: "rust_pair_completion_spelling_scaffold_trigger", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_unit_live_read", decl_name: "gunbc_runner_unit_live_read_absent_routing_scaffold", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.tools.card_intake", decl_name: "tcgplayer_money_measure_grounding_disposition", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.host.host_phase_status_witness", decl_name: "modeled_phase_fixture", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.lens.application_serializer", decl_name: "construction_justification", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.lens.enforcement.vocab", decl_name: "narrowing_reason_same_variant_disposition", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.decl_index", decl_name: "decl_facts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.lens.enforcement.cost_coverage", decl_name: "cost_coverage_fn_verdict_from_body", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.lens.complexity_lowering", decl_name: "cost_is_lowerable", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.lens.enforcement.inventory", decl_name: "cadence_scheduling_rows_for_witness", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.host.sccache_verified_install", decl_name: "sccache_verified_install_admitted_plan", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
